    "processingDescription": "Private complete schema-2 virtual-robot fixture. Geometry and the registered bilateral articulation convention come from the authored Numi dove mechanics; the 0.001 kg whole-body mass, body inertia, and 0.00001 kg membrane-wing inertial entries are an internally consistent ultralight ornithopter design, not biological measurements. The v9 robot has 0.900 m semi-spans and 1.200 m chords, with stroke angles reduced fivefold to preserve the compact fixture's peak spanwise membrane velocity. The declared hover actuator sets -0.04 rad pitch at the power-stroke phase knots and 0 rad at recovery. On Apple M4, the D24 five-cycle fixed-body D3Q19 screen selected this exact candidate (SHA256 9a4f1c36877fa9b1e7b540468529d95d6502e0476cc295c9042ff24da37ba5ab): mean aerodynamic force [-0.000813, 0.000000, 0.009879] N, versus 0.009810 N robot weight. The initial +4.706 degree body-y attitude trim aligns that screened resultant vertically; it does not prove free-flight stability. A full five-cycle fixed-body pre-roll followed by coupled six-DOF release failed its runtime Mach bound at release step 1251 (Mach 7.567), so v9 is not a flight-capable result and must not be used for training promotion. The next required mechanics are a coupled attitude/load controller and stable release validation, followed by 1/2/4 body-step refinement. This is a numerical D3Q19 robot calibration model, not a measured Deetjen or biological specimen."
